{#- The processes of a container's t3.service that a T3 restart would end and that are a user's (docs/reference/development-containers.md#the-restart-window).
    `lines` is the output of the restart phase's read in the container: `main <MainPID>`, then `pid ppid etimes comm` for each pid of
    t3.service's cgroup.procs. It fails closed: an unreadable read, a MainPID of 0 or one that is not in the service prints
    {"readable": false}.
    May go: systemd's MainPID of t3.service (T3); these direct children of it: the resource monitor, T3's own `git` (a terminal's git
    is a child of its shell), and a provider (`claude`, `codex`, the recipe's binary names); and each descendant of a provider that
    started within 10 s of the provider, the session's own setup such as its `sh` and stdio MCP servers.
    Counted as `terminals`: every other direct child of T3, a shell node-pty forked, open idle or running something.
    Counted as `commands`: every other process, such as what a terminal runs, a provider's descendant started later (a turn's tool,
    or a dev server an earlier turn left), or a process whose parent left the service (an orphan of a backgrounded command).
    Prints JSON {"readable": true, "terminals": n, "commands": n}. -#}
{%- set ns = namespace(main=0, readable=true) -%}
{%- set procs = [] -%}
{%- for line in lines -%}
  {%- set f = line.split(None, 3) -%}
  {%- if f | length == 2 and f[0] == 'main' and f[1] is match('^[0-9]+$') -%}
    {%- set ns.main = f[1] | int -%}
  {%- elif f | length == 4 and f[0] is match('^[0-9]+$') and f[1] is match('^[0-9]+$') and f[2] is match('^[0-9]+$') -%}
    {%- set _ = procs.append({'pid': f[0] | int, 'ppid': f[1] | int, 'age': f[2] | int, 'comm': f[3] | trim}) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set pids = procs | map(attribute='pid') | list -%}
{%- if ns.main == 0 or ns.main not in pids -%}
{{ {'readable': false} | to_json }}
{%- else -%}
{%- set by_pid = dict(procs | map(attribute='pid') | zip(procs)) -%}
{%- set providers = procs | selectattr('ppid', 'equalto', ns.main) | selectattr('comm', 'in', ['claude', 'codex']) | list -%}
{%- set provider_age = dict(providers | map(attribute='pid') | zip(providers | map(attribute='age'))) -%}
{%- set counts = {'terminals': 0, 'commands': 0} -%}
{%- for p in procs if p.pid != ns.main -%}
  {%- set walk = namespace(at=p.ppid, provider=0, depth=0) -%}
  {%- for _ in range(32) if walk.provider == 0 and walk.at in by_pid and walk.at != ns.main -%}
    {%- if walk.at in provider_age -%}
      {%- set walk.provider = walk.at -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- set walk.at = by_pid[walk.at].ppid -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- if p.ppid == ns.main and p.comm in ['t3-resource-mon', 'git', 'claude', 'codex'] -%}
  {%- elif walk.provider != 0 and p.age >= provider_age[walk.provider] - 10 -%}
  {%- elif p.ppid == ns.main -%}
    {%- set _ = counts.update({'terminals': counts.terminals + 1}) -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- set _ = counts.update({'commands': counts.commands + 1}) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{ {'readable': true, 'terminals': counts.terminals, 'commands': counts.commands} | to_json }}
{%- endif -%}
